WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Researchers can now analyze real-clawed usage data outside labs, andthropic-released privacy-preserved tools and 250,000 conversations for independent impact studies. This is Models &amp; Agents, episode 154, andthropic-opened aggregated-clawed conversation data from April and May, 2026, to Stanford Salt Lab, Oxford Human Information Processing Lab, and Metter. The analysis showed over half the chats involved consequent

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:54.900
financial tasks that affect others or prove hard to undo. OpenAI published its technical report on the hugging-face agent incident, along with third-party assessments from Metter and Redwood. Visa shipped an open-source agentic security harness that auto-remediates vulnerabilities before human review. Builders should watch how these data access and governance moves affect agent deployment decisions this week.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:18.840
Anthropic-released privacy-preserved clawed usage data and analysis tools to external researchers for the first time. Three independent groups examined 250,000 aggregated conversations from April and May, 2026. The company now invites additional researchers to apply for access via a public form to pursue studies previously possible only inside labs.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:41.900
This shifts AI-impact research from internal only to distributed across academia while keeping raw user data protected. Watch for follow-on papers and whether other labs adopt similar data sharing models. A new RRI-ZF survey catalogs 80-strict unsupervised post-training methods organized by the internal signal supplying the update.

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:57.380
The signals include prediction statistics, sample relations, self-generated targets, or internal evaluators. The paper maps how each choice of signal and task structure determines whether post-training improves the model or amplifies error.

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:12.100
An orthogonal input visibility by update persistence view defines deployment regimes and a unified selection framework. Builders working on post-training pipelines should test the catalog against their unlabeled data sources this week.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:24.760
Another RRI-ZF study tests stability of embedded steering for refusal suppression and brevity induction across five instruction tuned models from 3 billion to 14 billion parameters.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:40.400
The tests cover non-adversarial supervised fine-tuning and reinforcement learning from human feedback. Behavioral preservation tracks training data pressure while the weight edit itself survives with mean vector recovery of 0.004.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:52.640
Fine-tuning does not dismantle the steering mechanism even when behavior reverts. Teams using activation steering should revalidate behavioral effects after any downstream fine-tuning run.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:03:05.640
A third RRI-Z paper shows parallel English dialect corpora where modern language models encode dialectal texts unequally at tokenization, pre-training, post-training, and inference stages.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:14.900
The gaps appear across model families. Character level tokenization removes neither input nor output asymmetries nor accuracy gaps.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:28.280
Reward models exhibit contextual unstable dialect preferences during post-training. Developers targeting global audiences should measure dialect performance explicitly rather than assuming semantic equivalence holds.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:41.240
Visa opensource the vulnerability agentic harness that runs 11 stages to discover, verify, remediate, validate, and iterate on vulnerabilities using an abstract syntax tree call graph.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:48.840
The default flow writes candidate fixes to a working copy, then runs an adversarial validation panel at stage 11.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:56.360
The panel returns validated, failed, or needs review verdicts without bypassing team build test or review gates.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:06.100
It supports per-stage model choice across anthropic, open AI compatible, and open weight backends and ships with MTTA observability.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:11.520
The harness is intended for authorized operators on code they own in controlled environments.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:24.440
Operators must still fence repos and use scoped credentials. This builds directly on the agent reliability questions from yesterday by showing how operational controls can be embedded before deployment scales.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:37.100
A venture-beat piece argues that agent governance must be enforced at the operational data layer through role and attribute-based access, dynamic column masking, and session level audit logging.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:41.900
The approach treats the agent as a first-class principle with declared purpose.

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:53.840
Nine controls grouped under enforce, see, and prove, and unify and harden appear as executable policies already present in databases rather than prompt guardrails.

00:04:54.620 --> 00:05:00.740
EDB Postgres AI is positioned as the open foundation delivering these controls with data sovereignty.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:09.720
Teams running autonomous agents should map their current IAM rules to agent identities and declared purposes before scaling deployments.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:20.160
Cyber insurers are updating policies in response to autonomous agent incidents. They are shifting from traditional controls to new risk assessments around agent behavior.

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:25.840
The article notes the hugging face incident as a reference point for emerging coverage questions.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:34.260
Organizations deploying agents should review policy language for explicit agent identity and action scope clauses in the coming quarter.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:44.500
A towards data science post demonstrates replacing open search with typed tools, hard bounds, and an UN bypassable gate when walking a knowledge graph.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:52.520
Four models tested on a wrong prediction scenario show the bounded approach reduces hallucination while preserving useful traversal.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:58.800
Builders should prototype the gate pattern on any agent that currently receives unrestricted context windows.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:07.460
Another towards data science guide focuses on obtaining higher quality code rather than higher volume when collaborating with coding agents.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:13.120
It emphasizes structured prompts and review loops that surface intent mismatches early.

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:19.760
Developers using agents for code generation should adopt the workflow on their next non-trivial feature branch.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:27.620
Analysis of corporate documentation found 227 install commands pointing to code with no identifiable owner.

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:32.280
The pattern indicates agents can introduce unvetted dependencies at scale.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:38.180
Security teams should add provenance checks to agent-generated package lists before any merge.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.280
Okay, let's pop the hood on data layer governance for agents.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:48.660
Everyone talks about agent guardrails as prompt instructions or monitoring layers added after the model.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:59.560
In practice, governance that must survive autonomous planning and cross-system action lives inside the database itself through enforceable policies evaluated at query time.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.780
An agent declares a purpose at session start.

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:09.100
That purpose becomes an attribute the existing role an attribute based access engine already understands.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:16.800
The policy engine evaluates it exactly like department or clearance level, denying access before any data leaves the store.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:25.840
This adds no extra latency beyond the existing authorization check yet guarantees the rule cannot be bypassed by clever prompting or tool chaining.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:34.740
Row and column level security plus session audit logging capture exactly which agent acted for which user and under what declared purpose.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:39.860
The trade-off appears when agents need broad read access for legitimate exploration.

00:07:40.420 --> 00:07:45.700
You must either prescope the purpose narrowly or accept that some queries will be rejected at runtime.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:50.980
Use this approach when agents will modify production data or cross trust boundaries.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:58.880
Relay on prompt guardrails only for read only, low stakes assistance, where the blast radius stays inside a single conversation.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:05.300
The gotcha that bites most teams is assuming the model will self-enforce rules written in the system prompt.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:10.480
Once the agent can plan multi-step actions, only the data layer still holds.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:15.840
Apply for anthropics researcher access form if you study AI societal impact.

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:22.660
The 250,000 conversation data set lets you run analyses previously impossible outside labs.

00:08:23.300 --> 00:08:32.820
Clone visas vulnerability agentic harness and run it with stop after S9 on a test repo to see the serif output before enabling remediation.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:41.660
Prototype the typed tool plus gate pattern from the towards data science post on any agent that currently receives unrestricted web search.

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:51.840
Map your current IAM roles to agent identities and declared purposes using the nine controls in the EDB governance framework before scaling autonomous agents.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:57.780
More labs may follow anthropics data sharing model after the initial three group results publish.

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:03.940
Cyber insurers are expected to release updated agent specific policy templates in the next quarter.

